Here is an idea for a tool I have had for a while and was wondering what 
others (or the development team,)  might have to add to this...

----

Item: Sharping Stone

Purpose: To allow adventurers to improve the quality of a bladed weapon.

Useage: Characters would either use the meta command, #rub, or apply the
        stone to a weapon (implementation I leave to the development
        team).
        
Effect: Will improve the quality of a bladed weapon up to +3 (or so,) as
        the more you sharpen a blade the more metal you remove from it,
        making it more brittle and increasing the chance of it breaking.
        
        The stone could be used on cursed weapons to improve their
        qualities to that of a normal weapon. 

Possible Screen Character: _ or * where _ would represent a stone to large
        to carry, and a * would be a pocket sized stone. Both sized stones
        could be found in shops and store owners would charge if the stone
        were used in the shop.

Notes:  I don't know that a blessed stone of sharpening would allow the
        weapon to become blessed, but I can see how a cursed stone would
        damage a weapon.
        
        Maybe if a potion of oil were introduced to the game it could be
        applied to the stone to improve the quality of the stone a bit.
        And if there were a potion of oil then ... well I'll save that
        for another submission...
